diff --git a/CRISPCLOUD.md b/CRISPCLOUD.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..01fb90e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CRISPCLOUD.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# CrispCloud PDF extensions
+
+This feature branch extends the Apache-2.0 DartPDF14.0.0 toolkit for reuse
+by CrispCloud’s graphical application and standalone Dart CLI. Its upstream
+base is `87adaa022c5ed6b22ca3232b6cae4a03e8389e98`.
+
+## Shared operations
+
+`packages/pdf_operations` supplies typed byte-in/byte-out operations: inspect,
+text/search, ordered merge, extraction, rotation, reordering, deletion, image
+insertion, foreground watermarks, strict named AcroForm filling, and import of
+externally recognized OCR spans. It contains no Flutter, platform file I/O,
+network client, credential store, or model dependency. Hosts own persistence.
+
+See the package README for page syntax, coordinate conventions, field schemas,
+font coverage requirements and explicit encryption decisions.
+
+## Engine changes
+
+- Selected-page extraction retains supported form/navigation data in a fresh
+  document and removes destinations to omitted pages.
+- Invisible OCR layers can embed Unicode fonts and ToUnicode mappings; missing
+  glyphs are rejected. Existing form-style APIs provide Unicode appearances.
+- Flattening uses current annotation geometry after rotation or resizing.
+- The editor’s multi-source insertion accepts per-source passwords.
+
+Original licenses remain intact. Test fonts have their own notices. The
+CrispCloud-specific UI, storage, optional-store split and redaction restrictions
+live in CrispCloud; this repository retains the general-purpose engine APIs.
+
+## Validation
+
+Focused regressions are in `packages/pdf_document/test/crisp_*`,
+`packages/pdf_operations/test/`, and
+`packages/dart_pdf_editor/test/crisp_insert_password_test.dart`.
+The operations emitter and benchmark produce reviewable PDFs and bounded VM
+measurements. The matching source snapshot is also exercised by CrispCloud’s
+PDF workflow and independent parser: https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispCloud/pull/6.
+
+These features do not implement secure redaction, XFA editing, automatic OCR
+recognition, or universal complex-script shaping. Page deletion is incremental;
+extraction can retain unused data inside resources shared with selected pages.
